From 52408797f33b13404f1063c4bf8037ec77c4faaf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sheepsticked <72666364+Sheepsticked@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 08:05:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] QuectelAtCommand: AMI action with correlated
 QuectelAtResponse/QuectelAtDone events

Upstream: https://github.com/IchthysMaranatha/asterisk-chan-quectel @ 3d45c7f072131296a7e3c1a4faf5bb18751dbd87
Purpose: QuectelAtCommand action + QuectelAtResponse/QuectelAtDone events for Aster
         (protocol contract: docker/asterisk/patches/README.md in the Aster repository)

Mirror of the chan_dongle patch (0001-chan-dongle-at-command-events.patch, wdoekes@31eb619) on
this fork: apart from names, at_queue.[ch] and manager.h are identical in both drivers and the
at_command, at_response, do_monitor_phone() and manager code the patch touches has the same shape.

An AMI client sends one AT command to a device and receives the modem's answer through events
that carry the action's ActionID. Lines are attributed by the driver's own command queue, never
by timing:

- at_queue: a task carries the ActionID of the QuectelAtCommand that queued it (empty for every
  other task). at_queue_insert_actionid() sets the tag only after the command was written, so an
  action that fails with "Queue error" never produces an event. at_queue_actionid_done() emits
  the single QuectelAtDone of the head task and clears the tag, so nothing later is attributed to
  that ActionID. at_queue_flush() (disconnect, reset, restart) ends tagged tasks with
  Result: ERROR, Error: queue flushed; a tagged task removed for any other reason gets
  Error: task removed.
- at_command: at_enqueue_user_cmd_id() queues a CMD_USER task with the action's timeout, ahead
  of other pending commands, exactly like the "quectel cmd" CLI command does.
- at_response: for a tagged CMD_USER task every line that is neither the final result nor an
  unsolicited report is a QuectelAtResponse; OK ends the task with Result: OK, ERROR /
  +CMS ERROR / +CME ERROR with Result: ERROR and the line as Error. "+CME ERROR:" is added to the
  response table so that it is handled like "+CMS ERROR:" instead of being ignored until the
  command times out. The unsolicited reports are the same result types as in chan_dongle (in this
  fork RES_ORIG/RES_CEND/RES_CONF match "^DSCI:", "VOICE CALL:" and "MISSED_CALL:") plus
  RES_RCEND ("REMOTE CALL END"), which only this fork classifies.
- chan_quectel do_monitor_phone(): a response timeout emits Result: TIMEOUT before the existing
  handling disconnects and restarts the device.
- manager: the QuectelAtCommand action (EVENT_FLAG_SYSTEM) validates ActionID (1-63 characters
  [A-Za-z0-9._-]), Command (1-256 characters, no CR/LF) and Timeout (1-60 s, default 15) before
  the device lookup, then requires the device to be connected and initialized. The events escape
  CR/LF like manager_event_message().

Line endings: the upstream blobs of at_command.[ch], at_response.[ch], chan_quectel.c and
manager.c are CRLF although .gitattributes says "* text eol=lf". git apply normalizes a file
while reading it and writes it back with the attribute's ending, so this patch is an LF diff
against the normalized text and the six files come out LF after the patch (at_queue.[ch] and
manager.h are LF upstream).

Untagged user commands (CLI "quectel cmd") behave as before and emit nothing.
